!requirements.txt
# Showcase deliverables are tracked despite the global ignores above (*.txt, etc.) —
# a showcase dir is a curated, runnable artifact, so everything in it is committed...
!dx-agent-dev-showcase/**
# ...INCLUDING model artifacts (*.onnx/*.dxnn/*.pt): for retrain/export showcases the
# compiled .dxnn, DeepX export config/metadata, and retrained best.pt ARE curated
# deliverables, so a fresh checkout carries the real produced models (no recompile needed).
# Only environments, caches, and runtime-download dirs are excluded — a *directory* ignore
# below cannot be un-ignored by the `!**` rule above, so downloaded/model-zoo binaries that
# live under these dirs (e.g. a fork/game showcase's setup.sh downloads) stay uncommitted:
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/venv/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/.venv/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/dxnn_models/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/onnx_models/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/download/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/__pycache__/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/output/
dx-agent-dev-showcase/**/.venv_path
session-ses_*.md

